VAR_A=("<ol style=\"margin-left:24px\"><li><b>Gross landing value.</b> For each province and quarter, multiply the quantity landed for each fish category (mt \u00d7 1,000 = kg) by the <b>matching historical first-sale price</b> (\u20b1/kg) for the same period and province, then add across categories.</li>"
"<li><b>Value at risk.</b> Projected shortfall = seasonal benchmark \u2212 forecast, <b>only when the forecast is below</b> the benchmark (otherwise zero). Multiply that shortfall by the same matching price. <i>Example (illustrative): 180 mt \u00d7 1,000 \u00d7 \u20b1180/kg = \u20b132.4M.</i></li>"
"<li><b>What it means.</b> It is the <b>gross revenue tied to the missing landings</b>. It is not profit, not household income loss and not disaster damage, because it ignores costs and how fishers, traders and buyers adjust.</li>"
"<li><b>How we defend it.</b> We repeat the calculation with <b>alternative price sources</b> (first-sale vs unit-value proxy) and a <b>\u00b1 price range</b>, and check whether the <b>ranking of province\u2013category combinations stays stable</b>. Units and coverage are matched before multiplying.</li></ol>"
"<p style=\"margin-top:8px\"><span class=\"link\" data-go=\"s-var\">Open the V.5 value-at-risk builder \u2192</span></p>")
VAR_Q=[("How will you calculate gross landing value at risk?",VAR_A),
("So is that amount money that will be lost?","<ul><li>No. It is the <b>gross value at stake</b> if the projected shortfall happens, priced at historical first-sale prices.</li><li>Actual losses would need extra evidence: costs, prices responding to scarcity, catch switching to other species, and how much fishing activity really drops.</li></ul>"),
("Why the shortfall, and not a share of landings exposed to a hazard?","<ul><li>In our study the \u201cexposed\u201d part of landings is the <b>projected shortfall itself</b>: the tons expected to be missing compared with the usual seasonal level.</li><li>We do not assume a hazard removes a fixed share of the catch. The forecast already uses mangrove history and prior typhoon exposure where they add predictive value, so the shortfall comes from the evaluated forecast rather than an assumed percentage.</li></ul>"),
("Why historical prices instead of forecasting prices?","<ul><li>Price forecasting is outside our scope. Historical first-sale prices keep the valuation transparent and reproducible.</li><li>Price uncertainty is handled by the sensitivity check (alternative sources and a \u00b1 range), and we report whether the rankings change.</li></ul>")]
QA["value"]=VAR_Q
QA["algo"].append(VAR_Q[0])
